Z||000066||Oreif||04-04-2001||02:25 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by sjp777:<BR><B>If anybody thinks that having religion in schools would have prevented Columbine, you're kidding yourselves. More atrocities have been committed in the name of religion than for any other cause in the history of mankind. Have you heard of the Crusades or Jihad?</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Why do people only see the religion side of the initial post? The post was NOT about religion by itself. The post was to show that MANY things contributed to the problems we have today. Yes, MAYBE religion has a part, But the "Experts" who tell us what were doing wrong, the attitudes of the parents and teachers, the lack of respect for the schools, and the governments are as much to blame (if not more so). Please look at the entire message portrayed. <P>||||reg||1
